## logo-designer-skill

`skills/visual-identity/scripts/export.sh` is derived from the logo-designer-skill project and **has been
modified**. The changes are listed in the file's own header; in summary:

1. Fixed an aspect-ratio inconsistency — the `sharp` path scaled to a square canvas while
   the other four converters scaled by width, so non-square logos exported differently
   depending on which tool happened to be installed.
2. Added a guard rejecting SVGs that still contain live `<text>`.
3. Added a monochrome export.
4. Made the "no converter found" install hints platform-aware.

Source: https://github.com/neonwatty/logo-designer-skill

The SVG generation approach described in `skills/visual-identity/references/logo-generation.md` is also
adapted from that project. Its interview phase was deliberately not adopted; the
reasoning is recorded in that file.

